 "perUnitProvenance": "perUnit, where present, is spend per judged unit (the first call and any re-ask after a bad reply) as a line in the prompt's length: fixed + perKChar x thousands of prompt characters. Fitted on 2856 live units (rubric and pack, the gpt-5.6-luna, deepseek-3.2 and glm-5 panel) of a 624-run study on real-repository and lite tasks whose prompts averaged 67 to 84 thousand characters; spend tracked prompt length with a correlation of 0.84 to 0.98. highRatio is the 90th percentile of actual over fitted spend. A plan that knows its prompts uses perUnit; the flat mean and p90 above were measured on smaller prompts and underestimated that study by about 2 to 3 times per call."
